From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repair rmp-serde through gnrt, because no resolution can

`//chrome/browser/oxy/adblock/rs:adblock_engine_ffi` fails to link because
`third_party/rust/rmp_serde/v0_15:lib` does not compile:

    error[E0425]: cannot find function `read_data_u8` in module `rmp::decode`
       --> .../vendor/rmp-serde-v0_15/src/decode.rs:497:40
    error: aborting due to 24 previous errors

rmp 0.8.11 moved `read_data_*` out of `rmp::decode` as free functions and into
the sealed `RmpRead` trait. rmp-serde 0.15.5 predates that and calls them as
free functions. It declares `rmp = "0.8.8"`, so Cargo resolves 0.8.15: inside
the range its own author wrote, and incompatible with it.

Measured against the vendored trees rather than inferred. 24 errors, all
E0425, all `read_data_*`, nothing else -- so the incompatible surface is
exactly these functions. rmp 0.8.10 `src/decode/mod.rs:208` has the free
`pub fn`; 0.8.15 `:107` has the same body as a `#[doc(hidden)]` trait method.

THE THREE REPAIRS, AND WHY THIS IS THE ONE

Bumping rmp-serde is not available. adblock 0.9.8 declares `rmp-serde =
"^0.15"` non-optionally, 0.15.5 (2021-06-11) is the last 0.15.x and there will
not be another, and the next non-yanked release is 1.0.0 -- outside the range.
No published rmp-serde both satisfies adblock and builds against a current rmp.

Constraining rmp below 0.8.11 works and costs more than it looks. It pins the
decoder that parses adblock's serialized filter data at 0.8.10 (2021-02-02),
five releases back, in a manifest whose stated policy is that this step pins
nothing (`browser.lock.json` `third_party.adblock_rust`, issue #5). It also
needs `rmp` declared as a direct dependency of the `chromium` package purely
as a constraint, which moves it in gnrt's inherited-privilege walk from the
graph root. And it silently falsifies a patch that landed hours ago: 066
declares `[crate.rmp] extra_input_roots = ['../README.md']` because 0.8.15's
`src/lib.rs` opens `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`. 0.8.10's does
not, so the pin would leave 066 declaring a compile input that is not one.

Upgrading adblock is the eventual answer and is not this change. adblock
0.12.0 dropped rmp-serde entirely for flatbuffers, which deletes the problem
rather than working around it -- at the cost of four crates to vendor
(`flatbuffers`, `arrayvec`, `precomputed-hash`, `rustc-hash`), five epoch
bumps that invalidate 066's `cssparser-v0_29` and `selectors-v0_24`
declarations, a `v0_9` -> `v0_12` rename in the FFI's `BUILD.gn`, and a
rewrite of the FFI against a changed engine API. That is a decision about
which ad blocker Astro ships, not a link fix.

WHY A VENDORED CRATE CAN BE EDITED AFTER ALL

066's header and AGENTS.md both say editing a vendored crate is not an option
because the next `gnrt vendor` overwrites it. That is true of editing the tree
by hand and false of the mechanism: `chromium_crates_io/patches/<crate>-<epoch>/`
exists so an edit SURVIVES re-vendoring. `apply_patches` in
`tools/crates/gnrt/vendor.rs` runs on every download, and 17 crates in this
checkout already rely on it. Both statements are corrected in the same commit
as this patch.

The file this patch adds is that mechanism's input, not the edit itself, so
the vendored tree stays generated: sweep it and `gnrt vendor` reproduces the
patched crate. gnrt applies it with `-p6 --directory=<vendor dir>`, verified
here by replaying that exact invocation against a pristine 0.15.5 unpacked
from crates.io.

The content is upstream's own fix, lifted from rmp-serde 1.1.1 -- its import
line, its method-call form, and its `byteorder::ReadBytesExt::read_u8`
disambiguation, which is needed because `RmpRead` in scope makes a bare
`rd.read_u8()` ambiguous. Its own header carries the detail.

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/patches/rmp-serde-v0_15/0101-Backport-rmp-serde-1.x-s-RmpRead-migration-to-0.15.5.patch b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/patches/rmp-serde-v0_15/0101-Backport-rmp-serde-1.x-s-RmpRead-migration-to-0.15.5.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a6df645
--- /dev/null
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/patches/rmp-serde-v0_15/0101-Backport-rmp-serde-1.x-s-RmpRead-migration-to-0.15.5.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+From c7599b123d9c19d4a1dc8be80dccb3f85b50cf23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
+Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 05:05:43 +0300
+Subject: [PATCH] Backport rmp-serde 1.x's RmpRead migration to 0.15.5
+
+rmp 0.8.11 moved `read_data_u8`/`read_data_i8`/... out of `rmp::decode` as
+free functions and into the sealed `RmpRead` trait. rmp-serde 0.15.5 was
+published 2021-06-11, before that, and calls them as free functions in 24
+places. Its own declared constraint is `rmp = "0.8.8"`, so Cargo resolves
+0.8.15 -- semver-compatible with the range, API-incompatible with the crate
+that declared it:
+
+    error[E0425]: cannot find function `read_data_u8` in module `rmp::decode`
+       --> .../vendor/rmp-serde-v0_15/src/decode.rs:497:40
+    error: aborting due to 24 previous errors
+
+WHY PATCH RATHER THAN RESOLVE IT AWAY
+
+There is no published rmp-serde that both satisfies its dependant and builds
+against a current rmp. `adblock` 0.9.8 declares `rmp-serde = "^0.15"`, and
+0.15.5 is the last 0.15.x -- the next non-yanked release is 1.0.0, outside
+the range. Constraining rmp to <0.8.11 instead means pinning the decoder at
+0.8.10 (2021-02-02), five releases back, for a parser that reads adblock's
+serialized filter data.
+
+WHAT THIS IS
+
+Upstream's own fix, taken from rmp-serde 1.1.1, applied to 0.15.5. Three
+parts, all of them upstream's:
+
+  * `RmpRead` added to the existing `use rmp::decode::{...}` line, in the
+    position rmp-serde 1.1.1 puts it (its decode.rs:16).
+  * The 24 call sites rewritten from `rmp::decode::read_data_x(&mut self.rd)`
+    to `self.rd.read_data_x()` (1.1.1's decode.rs:460, 503-512, and the f32 /
+    f64 coercion arms).
+  * The local `read_u8` helper disambiguated to
+    `byteorder::ReadBytesExt::read_u8(rd)`. With `RmpRead` in scope, plain
+    `rd.read_u8()` is ambiguous between the two traits -- upstream hit the
+    same thing and made the same edit (1.1.1's decode.rs:365). Left alone
+    this is an E0034, not a silent change of behaviour.
+
+Nothing here is invented, and nothing changes what the decoder does: rmp
+0.8.11 moved these bodies into a trait without editing them, and the error
+type still lines up, since `ValueReadError<E = Error>` defaults to
+`std::io::Error` and the blanket `impl<T: std::io::Read> RmpRead for T` sets
+`Error = std::io::Error`.
+
+Removable once the ad blocker moves to adblock 0.12 or newer, which dropped
+rmp-serde entirely in favour of flatbuffers.
